<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Waleran III, Duke of Limburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1226">1226</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Waleran III (d. 1226) was Duke of Limburg from 1221, a son of Duke Henry III of Limburg. He was active in the struggles between the Welf and Staufen claimants to the German throne. In 1214 he married Ermesinde, heiress of Luxembourg; their son Henry founded the Luxembourg line, while Limburg passed to his son by his first marriage, Henry IV.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/waleran-iii-duke-of-limburg.jpg" alt="Waleran III, Duke of Limburg" width="198" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Augustin Calmet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waleran_III_of_Limburg.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
